00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:04.377
-Just play the game!

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.745
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:07.279
-You're doing the math
in your head, right?

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:08.481
There's a lot of Roots.

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:09.682
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:12.418
There's at least eight Roots,
yeah, yeah.

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:14.820
-That's some skrilla scratch,
Jimmy.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.388
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:17.556
-"I'm a newlywed, man.

00:09:17.556 --> 00:09:18.724
We're saving up."

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:19.891
Alright.
-Alright.

00:09:19.891 --> 00:09:22.094
Alright, here we go.
-Mm-hmm.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.262
-[ Exhales forcefully ]

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.263
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
Ah, I'm

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.564
[ Buzzer ]
in the Cheerios!

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.132
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.132 --> 00:09:28.634
-Honey Nut Cheerios?

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:29.768
I'm in the Cheerios.

00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:31.069
"Honey, I Shrunk the Kids."
-Yeah!

00:09:31.069 --> 00:09:32.237
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]
[ Ding]

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:34.440
♪♪

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.042
-You guys have been out, doing
all this press for the movie

00:09:37.042 --> 00:09:38.644
-Yeah.
-and you brought
something tonight

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.212
that's a surprise
for our audience.

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:41.447
-Yes.
The Lonely Island

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:44.216
kind of made a little gift
for you, actually.

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:45.518
You know, they put you
on these press tours,

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:47.753
you go like state to state
and you go to colleges

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.255
and you do junket days.

00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:50.456
And we were like,
"We need something

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:52.758
to sort of keep our sparks
flying a little,

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.860
something exciting to do
during the interviews.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.363
So we turned it
into a game where

00:09:57.363 --> 00:10:00.265
we would try and mention you
as much as possible,

00:10:00.265 --> 00:10:02.901
without anyone sort of knowing
that's what we were doing.

00:10:02.901 --> 00:10:05.337
[ Laughter ]
Because I knew I was coming here

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:06.972
at the end of everything

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:08.674
and then,
I could show it to you, so,

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.309
we put it together, hopefully.
-Are you kidding me?

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:11.377
This is awesome.
-And these are all real.

00:10:11.377 --> 00:10:12.644
These are all
different interviews.

00:10:12.644 --> 00:10:13.713
Each one's different, so.

00:10:13.713 --> 00:10:14.880
-I'm freaking out. Alright.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.881
-It's pretty great.
-Lonely Island, here.

00:10:15.881 --> 00:10:17.149
Check this out.

00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:18.784
-When we'd be writing,
we'd always say, you know,

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:20.586
It's like Jimmy Fallon
always says,

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:23.088
'If you think it,
put it in the show.'"

00:10:23.088 --> 00:10:24.456
-You know
what Jimmy Fallon says.

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:26.725
He always says,
"Truth is stranger

00:10:26.725 --> 00:10:28.059
than not truth."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.059 --> 00:10:29.828
-It's a weird way of phrasing
it, but that's Jimmy.

00:10:29.828 --> 00:10:31.997
Jimmy Fallon has a saying,
which is,

00:10:31.997 --> 00:10:33.565
"Never [bleep] in a volcano."

00:10:33.565 --> 00:10:35.300
[ Laughter ]
-He always says that.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.236
-You know
what Jimmy Fallon says --

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:38.337
'Dress for the job you want.

00:10:38.337 --> 00:10:39.505
In track suits."

00:10:39.505 --> 00:10:40.706
[ Laughter ]
-I haven't heard him say that.

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:42.408
-He says it a lot.
He says it a lot.

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:45.744
-Well, Jimmy Fallon always says,
"Wavelengths are like Earth --

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:46.879
everybody's on the same one."

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:48.047
[ Laughter ]
-Mm.

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:50.182
-I believe it was
Jimmy Fallon who said,

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:52.218
"Never look a gift whale
in the mouth."

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:54.653
-Yeah. Which we immediately
tried to correct him on,

00:10:54.653 --> 00:10:56.588
but he was not having it.
-Yeah, he was furious, actually.

00:10:56.588 --> 00:10:58.057
-Yeah.
There's no such thing

00:10:58.057 --> 00:10:59.658
as a gift whale.
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:01.693
You know, it's like
Jimmy Fallon always says --

00:11:01.693 --> 00:11:03.695
"Un elefante no es us perro."

00:11:03.695 --> 00:11:06.132
-Classic Jimmy Fallon.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.132 --> 00:11:08.500
-Well, like Jimmy Fallon
always says, you know,

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.703
"You can't teach a horse
to read Braille."

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:12.171
And we try to live by that.

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:13.439
-It's like Jimmy Fallon
always says,

00:11:13.439 --> 00:11:15.307
Always wear your beanie
like a Smurf."

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:17.176
It's like Jimmy Fallon
always says,

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:18.377
"Potato, potahto."

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:19.678
-Jimmy Fallon says that?

00:11:19.678 --> 00:11:22.581
-El protagonista de la próxima
película "Popstar,"

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:23.982
Andy Samberg.

00:11:23.982 --> 00:11:25.684
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:25.684 --> 00:11:27.485
-Yo soy Jimmy Fallon?

00:11:27.485 --> 00:11:29.822
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:29.822 --> 00:11:31.290
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.191
[ Cheering and applause ]
-You did it!
-Yeah.

00:11:33.191 --> 00:11:34.860
-How'd you do that?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.629
How did you do that?
You're the best.

00:11:36.629 --> 00:11:39.831
[ Rimshot ]

00:11:39.831 --> 00:11:41.967
Oh, man.
-It made perfect sense
in context.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:44.436
-I'm honored.
-In context, it made
perfect sense.

00:11:44.436 --> 00:11:45.438
[ Laughter ]
-I'm honored.

00:11:45.438 --> 00:11:46.705
Here's what you tweeted out.

00:11:46.705 --> 00:11:48.573
It's you and the writers,
working hard on the Emmys.

00:11:48.573 --> 00:11:50.008
-Yeah.
-That's you, face-down.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:51.977
You're planking. You're trying
to bring the plank back.

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.812
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Well, me

00:11:53.812 --> 00:11:55.013
and the Lonely Island guys

00:11:55.013 --> 00:11:57.583
decided that we wanted
to bring back planking

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:59.685
because it went away too soon,
don't you think?

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:01.620
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:02.620
[ Applause ]

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.057
It's like a lot of --

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:06.458
-I think it had a good run.

00:12:06.458 --> 00:12:08.026
You think it should come back?

00:12:08.026 --> 00:12:09.361
-I walk down the street
and I'm just looking

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:11.130
at a bunch of floopy cores.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.798
[ Laughter ]

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:14.299
-Floopy cores?
-Yeah.

00:12:14.299 --> 00:12:15.734
-You want people to plank more.

00:12:15.734 --> 00:12:17.970
-More planking, for surely.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:21.206
-Well, to people that don't know
what planking is...

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:22.641
-We could show.

00:12:22.641 --> 00:12:23.875
-Show everyone what a plank is.
-Okay.

00:12:23.875 --> 00:12:27.779
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:12:27.779 --> 00:12:29.381
-Do it right there.
I'll take this out.

00:12:29.381 --> 00:12:32.217
-So you gotta be super firm.
-Okay, yeah.

00:12:32.217 --> 00:12:34.419
[ Laughter ]
-[ Groaning ]

00:12:34.419 --> 00:12:36.788
-Oh, my God.
Your back okay?

00:12:36.788 --> 00:12:38.624
And you're 23 years old.

00:12:38.624 --> 00:12:39.725
-Look at that.

00:12:39.725 --> 00:12:41.259
-Oh, that's what planking is.
-Yeah.

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:42.261
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:44.763
#BringBackPlanking

00:12:44.763 --> 00:12:46.799
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:49.467
I thought of something.

00:12:49.467 --> 00:12:51.070
I thought of something.
-Yeah.

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:52.404
-You want to try a double plank?

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:54.139
-I would love to try that,
Jimmy.

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:56.041
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:58.277
I'm not sure what it is,
exactly,

00:12:58.277 --> 00:12:59.844
but I like the way it sounds,

00:12:59.844 --> 00:13:00.979
-I don't know where to --
-so I'm trusting you that it's

00:13:00.979 --> 00:13:02.748
going to be great.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:04.516
Whatever it is will be awesome.
-I'm trying to think of where --

00:13:04.516 --> 00:13:06.785
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:06.785 --> 00:13:08.653
-Pretty narrow desk,

00:13:08.653 --> 00:13:09.789
but I'm sure
you'll figure it out.

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:11.456
[ Cheering and applause ]
-[ Laughing ]

00:13:11.456 --> 00:13:12.624
-Oh, yeah.

00:13:12.624 --> 00:13:14.192
-I weigh a lot.

00:13:14.192 --> 00:13:16.161
-You're good.

00:13:16.161 --> 00:13:17.296
-Double plank.

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:19.832
-Planking is back!

00:13:19.832 --> 00:13:21.734
Planking is back!
-#PlankingIsBack

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:23.201
The double plank.
Hey, Roots,

00:13:23.201 --> 00:13:25.003
you want to try for a triple
plank, any of you guys?

00:13:25.003 --> 00:13:26.805
[ Cheering ]
Want to do it? Roots!

00:13:26.805 --> 00:13:28.006
-No, they're not into it.

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:30.642
-Roots!
-They're not into it.

00:13:30.642 --> 00:13:32.210
-That's alright.
They don't want to do it.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.747
Double plank -- never been done
on TV before.

